fix(bar,appearance): restore bar background + clear layout warnings

The bar rendered with no background (content floating on the
wallpaper) because Appearance.backgroundTransparency evaluated
undefined while appearance.transparency was still loading, which
NaN-poisoned the entire colLayer* pipeline. Optional-chain the
transparency reads with an opaque, non-automatic fallback.

Also resolved the cascade of layout warnings now that bars
actually instantiate:

- BarContent center section: top+bottom+verticalCenter was an
  over-specified anchor conflict; verticalCenter dropped (top
  and bottom already pin the vertical extent).
- BarGroup: gained showBackground/backgroundColor/backgroundRadius
  properties. BarContent now configures the center pill via these
  instead of injecting a child Rectangle, which the default alias
  was misrouting into the inner GridLayout (anchored item in a
  layout = undefined behavior).
- implicitWidth/Height ternaries returning undefined (BarWindow
  50/106, BarContent separator) now return 0; the inactive axis
  is governed by anchors/Layout.fill anyway.
- StyledPopup reparent loop now skips non-visual children
  (Connections/Timer/models have no `parent` property).

Shell loads with zero ano-code warnings; remainder are
third-party tray icons and system SVG theme issues.
